      en: "Grand Barbe is a prominent hill on Rodrigues Island, approximately 18 km northeast of Port Mathurin. Rising to about 396 meters, it is one of the highest points on the island. The hill is primarily composed of Miocene volcanic rock and is covered with endemic vegetation such as the Rodrigues dwarf palm. Hiking trails traverse dense forests where the rare Rodrigues flying fox (Pteropus rodricensis) can be observed. The summit offers panoramic views of the east coast and the coral reef. The area is part of the Grande Montagne Nature Reserve, established in 1950. Nearby limestone caves contain evidence of early human habitation.",
